    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42953" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sciāpŏdes</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scĭŏpŏdes</span></b> ), um,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκιάποσες,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a fabulous people
				in Libya</i>, <i>with monstrously large soles to
				their feet</i>, <i>which they were said to turn up
				and use as umbrellas</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 2,
				2, § 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol.
			8</span></i>; Aug. Civ. Dei, 16, 8.</div>
